# L §5.8: "The question is the text of the hole that the gap rule gives" (the first example input).  No row
# governs allowances[u18], so its read is the question (L §4.6 step 5, HOLE-UNGOVERNED), printed with the item
# and keys it came from (L §8.1).  The row for u5 is read.
# held: (L §8.2) "a row whose span has a start and no end ..., band rows included, read at a law date after the
# cut K": the law date is after the model's on, so every open-ended row read is listed.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index age_groups = [u5, u18, u24]

input allowances[g in age_groups]: money PLN question "Jaka jest kwota zasiłku dla tej grupy wieku?"

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  allowances[u5] = 95.00 PLN

ask q1: allowances[u5], allowances[u18] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (95.00 PLN, ?"Jaka jest kwota zasiłku dla tej grupy wieku?" (allowances[u18]))
  held: allowances[u5] = 95.00 PLN (v), read for 2026-06-30
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
